               "headline":  "Strong Q3 beat, but AI-chip selloff drags SITM below every EMA",
               "technical":  "SITM closed at $361.24 on 2026-11-20, down 10.83% in one session. It opened at $390.46 and finished near the day\u0027s low of $356.21. The trend is clearly down. Price sits far below the EMA 50 ($502.56), EMA 200 ($520.39) and EMA 100 ($538.68); EMAs are moving averages of price over 50, 100 and 200 days that give more weight to recent days. The EMA 50 has fallen beneath both longer averages, so the medium-term trend has turned lower. Momentum is weak. MACD 12/26/9, a trend-momentum gauge, is -34.82, just under its signal line at -34.45, and the histogram is a tiny -0.37. Selling is no longer speeding up, but there is no bullish turn yet. RSI 14 (a 0–100 momentum gauge; under 30 is oversold) is 33.8, close to oversold. Price is pinned to the lower Bollinger Band at $360.37; the bands sit about 2 standard deviations either side of the 20-day average of $437.38. In the 52-week range of $243.68–$901.81, price is about 18% up from the low and about 60% below the high. Volume was 940,600, or 1.14× the 20-day average, which confirms the selling but does not look like panic. Support is at $356–360; resistance is at $437, then about $503.",
               "fundamental":  "SiTime makes precision timing chips. In AI data centers, its MEMS oscillators and clocks sit inside optical modules, switches and accelerator cards. Q3 2026, reported on 2026-11-04, was strong: revenue was $298.7M (+257% y/y), non-GAAP gross margin was 70.7%, and non-GAAP EPS was $4.01 against a $3.41 consensus. Core comms/enterprise/data-center revenue grew 202% y/y to $127.3M. The Renesas timing unit (TPD), acquired on 2026-07-01, added $86.3M, and over 80% of that comes from data-center and comms customers. Q4 guidance is $331–341M revenue, about 70% gross margin and about $4.76 EPS. Management expects up to 2× more timing content in near-packaged optics and 3× in co-packaged optics, and puts its design pipeline at $10B. The weak spots: operating cash flow was -$6.6M, DSO (days to collect payment) rose to 61, and wafer supply stays tight into 2027.",
               "news":  [
                            "2026-11-04: Q3 2026 revenue of $298.7M and non-GAAP EPS of $4.01 beat consensus by about 3% and 18%, driven by AI-infrastructure timing demand and the acquired Renesas TPD. Even so, the stock was reported down about 10.7% after hours, a sign of how high expectations were.",
                            "2026-11-04: Q4 guidance calls for $331–341M revenue, about 70% non-GAAP gross margin and about $4.76 non-GAAP EPS at the midpoint. Management said wafer supply constraints will last into 2027.",
                            "2026-11-04: SiTime announced a 3-for-1 forward stock split. Holders of record on 2026-12-03 get two extra shares for each share held, and split-adjusted trading is expected to start on 2026-12-07.",
                            "The stock bounced to $457.05 on 2026-11-09, then slid 5.3% to $421.16 on 2026-11-16 and 3.3% to $405.10 on 2026-11-19. GuruFocus also notes about $501M of insider selling over the past 12 months, with no insider buying.",
                            "2026-11-20: SITM\u0027s 10.83% drop came during a sector-wide AI-chip selloff in which AMD, Micron and Broadcom each fell roughly 11–13%. Reports blamed AI-capex doubts, high valuations, rates and China/export-control worries; I found no SiTime-specific news that day.",
                            "I found no analyst rating or price-target changes for SITM between 2026-10-21 and 2026-11-21; the latest dated actions I found are from August 2026."
                        ],
               "caution":  "The trend is down on all three EMA timeframes. The stock is now trading on AI-chip sentiment rather than its own results: it fell after a clear beat on 2026-11-04 and again on 2026-11-20 with no company news. If the lower band near $360 and the $356 intraday low break, there is little chart support before the 52-week low of $243.68. Other things to watch: the $1.35B of 0% convertible notes, negative Q3 operating cash flow and $501M of insider selling. From 2026-12-07, the 3-for-1 split will divide quoted prices by three.",
               "opportunity":  "The business is moving the opposite way to the share price. Q4 guidance implies about 11–14% quarter-on-quarter growth with margins near 70%, and management expects more timing content per optical module as the industry moves to 1.6T and co-packaged optics. RSI at 33.8 is near oversold and price is hugging the lower Bollinger Band. That setup often comes before short-term relief bounces, but it does not guarantee one. The drop came from sector sentiment, not a broken moat. Getting back above the 20-day average near $437 would be the first sign the stock is stabilising.",
               "risks":  [
